# Pulse tick: `/seneschal brief` — the estate's FRONT DESK (dotfiles-front-desk-faty).
# Once a day, before Zig's morning, it answers "what needs Zig, everywhere" from
# live cross-repo reads and ends by ASKING him about the top of that list.
#
# ADVISORY ONLY, BY CHARTER. The seneschal holds no dispatch authority — the
# MARSHAL dispatches (seats.yml charter lines; dotfiles-seat-address-spec-uikg).
# This unit therefore injects a skill that reports and routes; if that ever grows
# hands, the unit is the wrong place to notice, so the brief carries an
# `advisory: true / authority: none` header and a suite asserts no other loop
# consumes it (agents/scheduler/test-seneschal-gather.sh).
#
# --session zig-computer: ONE session per server, named for the host (Zig's
# ruling 2026-08-09 — the separate `work` session is abolished, and
# session:window == host:seat universally).
#
# --fresh: warm process, COLD CONTEXT. A brief is a whole-fleet read with no
# dependence on yesterday's transcript, and a durable window that never clears
# would drift into the ceiling inside a week.
#
# NO --model FLAG ON PURPOSE. The pin is resolved from the roster
# (agents/seats.yml -> seneschal: model: fable) by pulse-inject itself
# (dotfiles-pulse-row-model-seat-d0bk). Passing --model here would SKIP the
# roster and fork the fact. ⚠️ The pin is spliced into the LAUNCH STRING, so it
# activates on a COLD LAUNCH only: a `seneschal` pane that is already warm keeps
# whatever model it was launched with, and pulse-inject logs that as a WARN
# rather than failing (wrong tier is visible after the fact and self-corrects on
# the next cold launch; wrong SEAT would not be, which is why only that one is
# fatal). Expect the first fire into a hand-opened window to be unpinned.
#
# Inspect runs: journalctl --user -u pulse-seneschal.service -n 20
[Unit]
Description=Pulse tick: /seneschal brief (the daily front-desk brief for Zig)

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=%h/.agents/agents/scheduler/pulse-inject.sh --loop %p --dir %h/dotfiles --session zig-computer --window seneschal --fresh --cmd "/seneschal brief"
